{"title":"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e88ddf64ced62ade514305ffd09e713671caf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (3,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c33a7cc0fae1ee840d254ddf69453f0092802244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fed0412b6502f9663cef129a2e092709a248f96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (5,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6de0c2ae1def8273ddd89f191309f7601ef5fe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> lie in the first quadrant and are the vertices of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. The quadrilateral formed by joining the midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b6691251a362837413262d094d29f92be951d579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is a square. What is the sum of the coordinates of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5e57006a283d0a19e8e872e91ffc556cfa0cb8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }7 \\qquad \\text{(B) }9 \\qquad \\text{(C) }10 \\qquad \\text{(D) }12 \\qquad \\text{(E) }16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"360\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cfb9d6da99381de67ea5f718469d0ecfdf8c71c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A=(3,9), B=(1,1), C=(5,3), D=(7,3); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,E); pair AB = (A + B)/2, BC = (B + C)/2, CD = (C + D)/2, DA = (D + A)/2; draw(AB--BC--CD--DA--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"205\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>We already know two vertices of the square: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/542ba3feaa128c288e33f1cfd80f481409409a74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A+B)/2 = (2,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d23b5ab0103f3cb676261b089126d473940d89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(B+C)/2 = (3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>There are only two possibilities for the other vertices of the square: either they are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/8144fc720051b8fbe49f359a72fec0072f0d044e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/9/799d02a02fb177ab095513b6c692834f9fe62b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, or they are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/1943d2c67bf92623b9dd5c81cbaa6a3968779217.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />. The second case would give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> outside the first quadrant, hence the first case is the correct one. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/8144fc720051b8fbe49f359a72fec0072f0d044e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, we can compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c5b781fdcb82abd6ded8810187e89d0715c9cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(7,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd0da8dd59d0b254ea1b015990d89471941350f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+3=\\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wR0mphUnhLc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wR0mphUnhLc</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we express the coordinates of the midpoints of the four sides.\n</p><p>Midpoint AB: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea9d3308a17610dcb38bfd84b443bdd0ea403605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Midpoint BC: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8790f46883a296366f038323844601dd2cde9ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Midpoint CD: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd3afde994a742a29957930a7e74cea32a017a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{a+5}{2},\\frac{b+3}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Midpoint AD: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04b9e4796f513e57823aeb313cd8d3609b431179.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{a+3}{2},\\frac{b+9}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Because the shape formed is a square, so we know that the distance between all four points are equal.\n</p><p>Using the distance formula on the two known coordinates, we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b0cd5579f5fe92e3b416e48adad56745de34787.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\\]\" width=\"229\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/53759ddb045c6d1b30e646a097ae832ce1696d95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\sqrt{(3 - 2)^2 + (2 -5)^2}\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/6/d96f65afef015617cea771cf0bed1b4b81ddf2db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\sqrt{1 + 9}\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5ed0c930ce2b75bc9df67eb59ebedd35534b27.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\sqrt{10}\\]\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Knowing the side length of the square, we use the coordinates of the midpoints of BC and CD. Substituting the coordinates of these two points, we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e411cf812eab56c37697aab77b57255d7c51a70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{10} = \\sqrt{(\\frac{a+5-6}{2})^2 + (\\frac{b+3-4}{2})^2}\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Squaring both sides and simplifying:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb7e59798775ae7d0054cb2ba0d1db2ad9395d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10 = (\\frac{a-1}{2})^2 + (\\frac{b-1}{2})^2\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf915fd60a501a9ebf01433ebfa480f74cafbc84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10 = \\frac{(a-1)^2 + (b-1)^2}{4}\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b8d4557747b2599cb0085e3bb75f53eda3ff986.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[40 = (a-1)^2 + (b-1)^2\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>After observation, we see that 40 is the sum of two squares: 4 and 36. It does not matter much to which one is which, so we have the following:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e32e77471c13d969e0eb2d22a2707e3c1022695.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-1)^2 = 4\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/0/180efb4bac932f0e797d7c5fbf9de89ea1bb2fca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(b-1)^2 = 36\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since, the question states that the four points lie in the first quadrant, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a316726fd8e11d2a6901b627f4fbe6dfc5472520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Then, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e19974c0735183b8f379c713b7ab7b504989002.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = 3\\]\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8b7a7fa68f0509ffb3f5c48036470c2645767f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b = 7\\]\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9aa4a39af420543b8010632f37b0c34823618fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = 3 + 7 = \\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"160\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Kellan Zhang (ThePlenGuy)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12\">2001 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017194843\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 304/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7670/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.426      1 -total\n 59.77%    8.623      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.81%    5.455      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7858:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017194843 and revision id 288755. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}